(4805893, 693726, 25890, '<td valign="top">Clean exposure. However, the combination of the large expanse of featurless, uniform sky, straight-on point of view and the dull light which results in cold colors dominating the frame from front to back leads to a flat image without any sense of depth (As in lack of what I call "layers of interest").</td>', 'Clean exposure. However, the combination of the large expanse of featurless, uniform sky, straight-on point of view and the dull light which results in cold colors dominating the frame from front to back leads to a flat image without any sense of depth (As in lack of what I call "layers of interest").', '2008-07-05 22:52:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(4805941, 692201, 25890, '<td valign="top">Good, balanced composition. However, the overall design suffers due to the presence of cars (I always find them ruinous to images of this type) and of people in brightly colored clothes right along a major leading line. Overcast weather is good for close-ups and texture shots, but not so suitable for wider views like this. Spot lighting (As in a bit of sunlight peeking throuh a crack in the clouds and hitting the building) would have elevated this image to a whole new level...Well, I am never patient or determined enough to just sit there for hours and hope that that would happen, myself. So I shouldn''t preach either.</td>', 'Good, balanced composition. However, the overall design suffers due to the presence of cars (I always find them ruinous to images of this type) and of people in brightly colored clothes right along a major leading line. Overcast weather is good for close-ups and texture shots, but not so suitable for wider views like this. Spot lighting (As in a bit of sunlight peeking throuh a crack in the clouds and hitting the building) would have elevated this image to a whole new level...Well, I am never patient or determined enough to just sit there for hours and hope that that would happen, myself. So I shouldn''t preach either.', '2008-07-05 23:17:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(4805991, 691674, 25890, '<td valign="top">I can''t decide if I like the stop-action or if I''d rather see some motion blur (Maybe combined with rear-curtain sync flash?) that emphasizes the energy and excitement in the game. I don''t have anything against selective desat, in general. I just don''t think that it adds anything to this particular image.</td>', 'I can''t decide if I like the stop-action or if I''d rather see some motion blur (Maybe combined with rear-curtain sync flash?) that emphasizes the energy and excitement in the game. I don''t have anything against selective desat, in general. I just don''t think that it adds anything to this particular image.', '2008-07-05 23:34:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(4806024, 693484, 37719, '<td valign="top">eart?  What is that?  Sorry, nice shot, but the fact that you couldn''t spell your title correctly just rubs me wrong.  I would like to have seen the horizon a little lower in the shot or perhaps cropped closer on the bottom.</td>', 'eart?  What is that?  Sorry, nice shot, but the fact that you couldn''t spell your title correctly just rubs me wrong.  I would like to have seen the horizon a little lower in the shot or perhaps cropped closer on the bottom.', '2008-07-05 23:56:38.000000', NULL, 1),
