(4808833, 691726, 30861, '<td valign="top">The framing on this one is immensely appealing to me, and moves it beyond the typical bike-shot to something much more dynamic and intriguing. The hyper-saturation of the colors is perfect for this subject as well. Nicely done.</td>', 'The framing on this one is immensely appealing to me, and moves it beyond the typical bike-shot to something much more dynamic and intriguing. The hyper-saturation of the colors is perfect for this subject as well. Nicely done.', '2008-07-07 10:13:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(4808834, 692141, 30861, '<td valign="top">Love the PP here, that will come as no surprise. Unfortunately, to my eye there''s a huge leveling problem going on here, and it''s a strange one:<br/> <br/>The image FEELS as if it is leaning over tot he right significantly. I ran some guidelines on it to check, and in fact he horizon itself is very nearly spot on level. But the other horizontal elements are all off kilter slightly, and all stacked tot he right side pretty much, so it just FEELS leany in a very uncomfortable way to me. I used skew adjustment to make it feel "right", and when I had finished that the horizon was tilted a little bit the other way, but overall the balance seemed better.<br/> <br/>I''ll be interested to see if others comment on this. I gave you a very good score regardless, this just nags at me. Feel free to PM me if you wish to discuss, I am done with the voting on this image so anonymity does not matter here.</td>', 'Love the PP here, that will come as no surprise. Unfortunately, to my eye there''s a huge leveling problem going on here, and it''s a strange one: The image FEELS as if it is leaning over tot he right significantly. I ran some guidelines on it to check, and in fact he horizon itself is very nearly spot on level. But the other horizontal elements are all off kilter slightly, and all stacked tot he right side pretty much, so it just FEELS leany in a very uncomfortable way to me. I used skew adjustment to make it feel "right", and when I had finished that the horizon was tilted a little bit the other way, but overall the balance seemed better. I''ll be interested to see if others comment on this. I gave you a very good score regardless, this just nags at me. Feel free to PM me if you wish to discuss, I am done with the voting on this image so anonymity does not matter here.', '2008-07-07 10:13:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(4808837, 692444, 30861, '<td valign="top">I think this is a wonderful image, so deadpan and understated. I can''t see a thing I''d change, including the slight cutting off of the hats left and right, which I think is priceless. I''m assuming you''re not doing very well, score-wise, and that''s a crying shame. This image is just completely fascinating, metaphorical as all get out. Is it an air show or are they waiting for the shuttle to land? Both occurred to me as "explanations", but of course i do not need one...</td>', 'I think this is a wonderful image, so deadpan and understated. I can''t see a thing I''d change, including the slight cutting off of the hats left and right, which I think is priceless. I''m assuming you''re not doing very well, score-wise, and that''s a crying shame. This image is just completely fascinating, metaphorical as all get out. Is it an air show or are they waiting for the shuttle to land? Both occurred to me as "explanations", but of course i do not need one...', '2008-07-07 10:16:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(4808839, 693722, 30861, '<td valign="top">Beautifully done. Love the overhanging branch on the left lower portion :-)</td>', 'Beautifully done. Love the overhanging branch on the left lower portion :-)', '2008-07-07 10:17:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(4808840, 693720, 30861, '<td valign="top">EXCELLENT! Well seen. I hope it''s scoring well, though I suspect it will be "underappreciated"...</td>', 'EXCELLENT! Well seen. I hope it''s scoring well, though I suspect it will be "underappreciated"...', '2008-07-07 10:17:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(4808846, 691954, 30861, '<td valign="top">Outstanding image. It draws me in, makes me want to read it cover-to-cover. It''s reminiscent of the great jjbeguin crowd-shot of a few years ago, though of course it''s completely different. But it has that same quality of the single face in the crowd sucking you in irrevocably.<br/> <br/>My only problem with this is that it''s not quite sharp enough, crisp enough. Still, hell of an image.</td>', 'Outstanding image. It draws me in, makes me want to read it cover-to-cover. It''s reminiscent of the great jjbeguin crowd-shot of a few years ago, though of course it''s completely different. But it has that same quality of the single face in the crowd sucking you in irrevocably. My only problem with this is that it''s not quite sharp enough, crisp enough. Still, hell of an image.', '2008-07-07 10:20:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(4808848, 691690, 39430, '<td valign="top">She looks a lot like this shot...<a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=691689" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/881/120/691689.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/881/120/691689.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/881/120/691689.jpg"/></a>.  This is a much better shot though.  I''d like to see more shadow detail (not THERE, just in general)  Pretty much everything but the reflection highlights disappears on my calibrated monitor.</td>', 'She looks a lot like this shot....  This is a much better shot though.  I''d like to see more shadow detail (not THERE, just in general)  Pretty much everything but the reflection highlights disappears on my calibrated monitor.', '2008-07-07 10:21:28.000000', NULL, 1),
