(4811600, 691155, 65234, '<td valign="top">I don''t disagree at all with your choice between those two shots.  I meant more a composition where she was looking/smiling at what I thought might be the groom in the background.  Sort of an, "Oh, joy, I see my beloved" pose which would cause me to think they were about to do the stereotypical run into each others'' arms thing.  In other words, I thought positioning her to the right of him (or what I imagined to be him) in the frame would tell a better story, in my imaginative mind ;-)  But glad to hear the bride was thrilled; surely her opinion counts way more than mine!  And you got some terrific shots while trashing the dress; great stuff.</td>', 'I don''t disagree at all with your choice between those two shots.  I meant more a composition where she was looking/smiling at what I thought might be the groom in the background.  Sort of an, "Oh, joy, I see my beloved" pose which would cause me to think they were about to do the stereotypical run into each others'' arms thing.  In other words, I thought positioning her to the right of him (or what I imagined to be him) in the frame would tell a better story, in my imaginative mind ;-)  But glad to hear the bride was thrilled; surely her opinion counts way more than mine!  And you got some terrific shots while trashing the dress; great stuff.', '2008-07-08 11:19:16.000000', NULL, 0),
