(5197694, 691011, 30861, '<td valign="top">I''m guessing this is the skull of a Desert Bighorn Sheep? Resting upside down? I see an eyesocket at the bottom, I see what I take to be the upper-jaw teeth, I see to undercurved, heavy horns... Am I right?</td>', 'I''m guessing this is the skull of a Desert Bighorn Sheep? Resting upside down? I see an eyesocket at the bottom, I see what I take to be the upper-jaw teeth, I see to undercurved, heavy horns... Am I right?', '2009-01-17 00:50:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(5199816, 692445, 66635, '<td valign="top">Awesome shot!</td>', 'Awesome shot!', '2009-01-17 16:47:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(5201739, 691011, 76217, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Bear_Music:</b></div><hr/><i> I''m guessing this is the skull of a Desert Bighorn Sheep? Resting upside down? I see an eyesocket at the bottom, I see what I take to be the upper-jaw teeth, I see to undercurved, heavy horns... Am I right? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You are correct, that is exactly the illusion I (or perhaps, better, the chameleon) was trying to create, a Southwestern Rock Chameleon photo that  "appears" to be a Desert Bighorn Sheep, resting upside down.<br/> <br/>That''s why these little critters are so elusive and hard to photograph - they can look like just about anything. I''ve actually got 12 or 13 of them and my portfolio and you''d never know it. ;)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-01-18 12:03:57.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Bear_Music: I''m guessing this is the skull of a Desert Bighorn Sheep? Resting upside down? I see an eyesocket at the bottom, I see what I take to be the upper-jaw teeth, I see to undercurved, heavy horns... Am I right?   You are correct, that is exactly the illusion I (or perhaps, better, the chameleon) was trying to create, a Southwestern Rock Chameleon photo that  "appears" to be a Desert Bighorn Sheep, resting upside down. That''s why these little critters are so elusive and hard to photograph - they can look like just about anything. I''ve actually got 12 or 13 of them and my portfolio and you''d never know it. ;)', '2009-01-18 11:44:27.000000', '2009-01-18 12:03:57.000000', 0),
(5213758, 692007, 66384, '<td valign="top">Love the way the colors run together. I especially like the greens. The image as a whole is wonderfully sunny and happy.</td>', 'Love the way the colors run together. I especially like the greens. The image as a whole is wonderfully sunny and happy.', '2009-01-23 01:34:43.000000', NULL, 0),
